     "content": {
      "size": 140379,
      "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
      "text": "[{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792379820,\"headline\":\"7Up launches classic soda that Coca-Cola doesn't have\",\"id\":142992181,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"The iconic soft drink company begins bottling a soda that was invented about 90 years ago.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=49f31d327e5eb82b84c55bbf18cb2cd9667b4535d85f3478a9255e8a13911231\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792366040,\"headline\":\"The Winners Inside SCHD - October 2026\",\"id\":142992053,\"image\":\"\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"SeekingAlpha\",\"summary\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=338e046f3cae53ba7d15e9918dd078db2c4d26bc477673975dbc84454a9e73f7\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792344300,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola Yields 2.3% and Nike Yields 4.4%. Here's Why Only 1 of These High-Yield Dividend Stocks Is a Buy This October.\",\"id\":142987940,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Investors must weigh the pros and cons before making a selection.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=9d2f4fcfaca53c99775ac5d6335f6eee5d06290c7b87eb84cdbfde8bc1da8081\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792317735,\"headline\":\"Sydney Sweeney Drops Second Nude Betting Ad as Powerade Fires Back\",\"id\":142986260,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Powerade’s “Never Just Sports” campaign responds to Novig’s Sydney Sweeney-led advertising. Novig claims first-time depositors increased by more than 218% around its campaign launch. The ...\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=7196a4c6512cbc5850de12c12dde368d14a948e2e21c3cfdb20ca0653bfae973\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792301807,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola Stock Is Up 39% in a Year. Here’s What’s Driving the Rally\",\"id\":142984390,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Key TakeawaysCoca-Cola stock is up 39% over the past year to a $94 close on October 16, after KFC picked Coke as its beverage partner for 3,718 US restaurants. The Street’s $95 mean target sits only 1% above the close.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=feae6a8327e5f3ee8c8203d9ef1004cdb58189647bf848756a226e5ad42bf3f0\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792293844,\"headline\":\"Yum! Brands (YUM) Resets KFC U.S. Drinks With A New 2027 Beverage Deal\",\"id\":142967243,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Yum! Brands (NYSE:YUM) unit KFC U.S. plans to shift its fountain beverage supplier to The Coca-Cola Company starting in 2027. The agreement will introduce Coca-Cola beverages across KFC restaurants in the United States as part of the chain's comeback plan. KFC U.S. is tying the new drink lineup to menu refresh efforts that aim to lift the in-store customer experience. This upcoming KFC U.S. and Coca-Cola beverage switch is one factor to weigh against the rest of our Yum! Brands analysis...\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=946dbddd36c03372c872922fa1ae4d4b4ce9199ce84240f130df12ef332a0e84\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792240099,\"headline\":\"In 1918, Milton Hershey Quietly Put About $60 Million In Stock Into A Trust. Over 100 Years Later, That Trust Still Exists And Holds About $23.6 Billion In Assets. Wealthy Donors Still Use A Similar Strategy, And The Legal Work To Set One Up Starts At A Few Thousand Dollars\",\"id\":142960721,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"A childless candy maker secretly handed his fortune to orphans in 1918, and the legal structure he chose still controls one of America's biggest snack companies today. Wealthy donors quietly use a version of the same playbook, but the fine print carries some serious surprises.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=f46826d92814f67f6093beab22199f6eff61c7b0e11730550f1f3e2df92d9c65\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792236000,\"headline\":\"When the Stock Market Gets Dangerous, These 6 Investments Have a History of Holding Up\",\"id\":142960010,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"These companies generate resilient revenues, which help make their stocks less volatile during market downturns.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=c3bb8900b1fbc403ac7002346e83167ebd87153a0b81791527a07965c14cc25b\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792217274,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola (KO) Will Supply Drinks At KFC U.S. Starting In 2027\",\"id\":142959156,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"KFC U.S. has selected Coca-Cola (NYSE:KO) as its exclusive beverage supplier, replacing PepsiCo across its U.S. restaurants. The new U.S. fountain partnership is set to begin in 2027, ending a multi decade relationship between KFC and PepsiCo. The agreement gives Coca-Cola expanded brand exposure within a major U.S. quick service chain as KFC refreshes its menu and drink lineup. The KFC U.S. switch to Coca-Cola fits into a wider set of shifts in foodservice partnerships that recent research...\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=fa9039af345745ede41b1f07fca6c047cc830aeca7dd7e9393c8de8e03c4819c\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792195081,\"headline\":\"Warren Buffett Paid About $1.3 Billion for Berkshire's Coca-Cola Shares. They're Now Worth About $37 Billion.\",\"id\":142954171,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Can a buyer near today's record high expect anything like Berkshire's result?\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=b4f263143251f43bc18fc7ab3991e19b839212ccde0dece216f8d12ad0d67bba\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792183507,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola (KO) Ascends While Market Falls: Some Facts to Note\",\"id\":142950854,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Coca-Cola (KO) closed at $93.52 in the latest trading session, marking a +1.65% move from the prior day.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=7e2911a8337ff5dea7b7f8755e4cc12d0d670b4d41df93cfe35962ec78eed898\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792180516,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola or Duke Energy: Only One Gets My Dividend Dollars for the Next 20 Years\",\"id\":142960016,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Key TakeawaysDuke Energy yields 3. 8% to Coca-Cola’s 2.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=bb1b3a4a8c4de5d04cda146cd4830e10053acad21769ad37cf695085eb2496dc\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792180362,\"headline\":\"PEP Stock Alert: KFC Just Dealt PepsiCo a Blow With New Coca-Cola Deal\",\"id\":142957860,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"KFC’s U.S. business is switching from Pepsi to Coca-Cola beginning in January. Here’s what the announcement means for PEP shares.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=fd1920e3c5f02f0728d248487562a1bc2225d60e8bca5777647166a652146dcc\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792179933,\"headline\":\"PepsiCo Is Down 25% From Its 52-Week High and Losing KFC to Coke. Here’s Where the Stock Could Go by 2030\",\"id\":142950856,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Key Stats for PepsiCo StockCurrent Price: $128. 38Target Price (Mid): ~$181Street Target: ~$142Potential Total Return: ~41%Annualized IRR: ~8.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=9d678a0ffa84bde60f6c3b240c8917d98f2bb92e2396f23d644e5b9327b23790\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792179794,\"headline\":\"9 Dow Jones Stocks Make Bullish Moves In A Defensive Market Rotation\",\"id\":142950007,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"A week that tested the financial markets showed the resilience of Dow Jones stocks. Apple and Coca-Cola were among nine standouts.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=af9cc9e28f3a10ea2145e9aa2ce346b5f10ea949ca6edd0654727a5baaf6a007\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792179754,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola Hit a 52-Week High on October 15. Here’s Where the Stock Could Go by 2030\",\"id\":142950855,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Key Stats for Coca-Cola StockCurrent Price: $92. 00Target Price (Mid): ~$107Street Target: ~$95Potential Total Return: ~17%Annualized IRR: ~4% / yearWhat Happened?The Coca-Cola Company (KO) touched an intraday 52-week high of $94.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=d303d7070e062f4d52d8dee08faffbcf90a5c26cb059935b6649bb006ec71e11\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792174616,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola (KO): Is Zero Sugar Creating New Demand or Shifting Existing Sales?\",\"id\":142950086,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"The Coca-Cola Company (NYSE:KO) earns revenue from beverage concentrates and finished drinks through its bottling network. Coca-Cola Zero Sugar volume grew 16% in the second quarter of 2026, while the wider Coca-Cola trademark grew 5%. Switching existing drinkers between products offers less earnings upside than recruiting customers or adding occasions. With its global brands and […]\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=9d89bf753816b301ee5016a1dddfffc9b537678507e4474142ecfa2147e2043a\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792173180,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola, Visa and Mastercard Hit Records as Investors Rotate Out of Chip Stocks\",\"id\":142950011,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Coca-Cola, Visa and Mastercard are among the stocks hitting records as investors look beyond the AI trade. Earnings could help broaden the rally.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=4ad8f758684d92953fbd2de585f964a4e73e883937172f558367ac5c9e40beba\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792172928,\"headline\":\"Sector Update: Consumer Stocks Mixed Friday Afternoon\",\"id\":142949086,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Consumer stocks were mixed Friday afternoon, with the State Street Consumer Staples Select Sector SP\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=41664e5551c462ec7e0fc84f3859445eb2a87655bcf0b5cf200084d5d6525846\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792169360,\"headline\":\"Coca-Cola Tops Buy Point After Landing A Whale. Four Other Top Stocks In Buy Zones.\",\"id\":142949143,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Coca-Cola rose above the 92.49 buy point of a flat base. It was among the actionable stocks Friday.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=e0a48e2e6def1f2fc47bda657b08ade7c7349141194884aa1667e412ada09923\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792167427,\"headline\":\"What Is Going On With PepsiCo Stock?\",\"id\":142949145,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"PepsiCo (PEP) stock trades at 16.1 times earnings. The median S\\u0026P 500 company, by contrast, trades at 22.8 times earnings. Over the past year, PepsiCo shares lost 11.9%, while the S\\u0026P 500 returned 17.9%. This underperformance occurred even as the company posted higher sales, margins, and cash flow in the twelve months to September 5, 2026. The market is either overlooking an improving business, or accurately pricing a company with stalled growth. What does a buyer get at this price.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=a6df16beffc601dd6f4b7d21b67062f4f10e72ccb790ee3030e036ea6329dd95\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792163917,\"headline\":\"Barclays Maintains Overweight on Coca-Cola, Raises Price Target to $98\",\"id\":142961236,\"image\":\"\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Benzinga\",\"summary\":\"Barclays  analyst Lauren Lieberman   maintains Coca-Cola (NYSE:KO) with a Overweight and raises the price target from $93 to $98.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=7695ebfb1de6fb17adb473c78c5106d4fb08a0ab8ca9f8bd7f3546674244812e\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792159584,\"headline\":\"KFC breaks up with Pepsi, signing Coke as its new drink provider\",\"id\":142948007,\"image\":\"https://s.yimg.com/rz/stage/p/yahoo_finance_en-US_h_p_finance_2.png\",\"related\":\"KO\",\"source\":\"Yahoo\",\"summary\":\"Kentucky Fried Chicken — a subsidiary of Yum! Brands (YUM) — just signed a deal for Coca-Cola (KO) to be its new beverage provider in the US, replacing PepsiCo (PEP). Yahoo Finance Executive Editor Brian Sozzi outlines the loss this represents for the US drink manufacturer.\",\"url\":\"https://finnhub.io/api/news?id=2f2c99d0354c0229d934afba5d5df49b3f20d0ee32c62a3deefa2623aa939c13\"},{\"category\":\"company\",\"datetime\":1792159542,\"headline\":\"KFC Signs Deal With New Soda Supplier in a Blow for PepsiCo\",\